// Fixed in 0.30.2 (F34.4, const.exit at the definition, front/check/names.vl const_body_exits): was RT-407: (RT-407's mechanism, eval_array_len) an array repeat's length `[0u8; (true || return) as usize + 1]` is accepted and the program prints 2; rustc refuses it (E0572, return statement outside of function body) (0.30.2)
// Found while writing RT-407 (consteval's eval_array_len, which the
// re-review of g302copy-148 names). Since v0.30.1 at least; the release
// build the same. rustc E0572 at the `return` (the rustc twin of this
// file). With an `if (true || return) { 2 } else { 3 }` length the
// program is refused as "not a compile-time constant". Siblings: rt_407,
// rt_407b, rt_407c, rt_407e.
// ERROR: line 11
// ERROR-COUNT: 1
fn main() {
    let a = [0u8; (true || return) as usize + 1];
    println("{}", a.len());
}
